BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261124T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261124T160000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research Cite It Right with NoodleTools @ 3p
 m\, Nov 24th
DESCRIPTION:Join SRJC Librarian Canon Crawford to learn how to simplify c
 itations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the way\, score quic
 k tips on finding credible research in the library and on the Web.NoodleT
 ools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliographies\, and offer
 s note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\, including the ca
 pability to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details: Extra Credit a
 vailable!This NoodleTools workshop will use APA and/or MLA style as live 
 demo examples\, depending on the participants that register.Don't worry! 
 Jessica will share how to use both MLA and APA. You're covered!You will l
 earn how to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide exam
 ples to show how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check fo
 r errors.Along the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credi
 ble research in the library and on the web.Check with your instructor to 
 confirm the citation style appropriate for your research assignment.Extra
  Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and 
 course name when you register if you would like us to notify your instruc
 tor that you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can wo
 rk with your instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your
  attendance.Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This w
 orkshop requires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting
 .You will receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this wo
 rkshop. Check your spam folder if you do not see it.This Zoom workshop wi
 ll open 10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked 
 to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch thi
 s 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with 
 an SRJC Librarian!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join SRJC Librarian Canon Crawford to learn 
 how to simplify citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the
  way\, score quick tips on finding credible research in the library and o
 n the Web.<br />NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bib
 liographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing feat
 ures\, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.<br />Wor
 kshop Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools workshop wil
 l use APA and/or MLA style as live demo examples\, depending on the parti
 cipants that register.<br />Don't worry! Jessica will share how to use bo
 th MLA and APA. You're covered!<br />You will learn how to sign up for an
  account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show how to create
  citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.<br />Along the w
 ay\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible research in the 
 library and on the web.<br />Check with your instructor to confirm the ci
 tation style appropriate for your research assignment.<br />Extra Credit:
  As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course n
 ame when you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that
  you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with 
 your instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attenda
 nce.<br />Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)<br />Th
 is workshop requires registration in order to be admitted to the Zoom mee
 ting.<br />You will receive a confirmation email with the Zoom URL link f
 or this workshop. Check your spam folder if you do not see it.<br />This 
 Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes early to allow you time to log on.<br 
 />Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.<br />Not f
 amiliar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoom meetin
 g.<br />Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
