SUMMARY:Cite It Right with NoodleTools: MLA APA @ noon\, Dec 2nd (in-pers
 on)
DESCRIPTION:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliog
 raphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features
 \, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Deta
 ils: Extra Credit available!You will learn how to sign up for an account 
 with NoodleTools. We will also provide examples to show how to create cit
 ations\, create a bibliography and check for errors. There will be time t
 o ask questions at the end of the overview —bring your sources along. J
 oin us for a workshop and learn how to cite your sources right!Extra Cred
 it: As students\, you have the option to submit your instructor and cours
 e name when you register if you would like us to notify your instructor t
 hat you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work wi
 th your instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your atte
 ndance.Registration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This worksh
 op does not require registration. However\, registering will guarantee ad
 mittance to this in-person workshop. Please arrive promptly.Workshop Loca
 tion: Santa Rosa Campus\, Doyle Library\, Room 4327. See map for directio
 ns to Doyle Library.The workshop will open 5 minutes prior to the start t
 ime.Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct policy.Have ques
 tions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
